d Wolfenstein let's  set the scene the main character in the  Wolfenstein series is BJ blast kovitch I  didn't name him that but I'm sure going  to make cheap BJ gags okay the  first-person shooter is one of the  longest-running in history but things  are set to change as Wolfenstein  introduces Youngblood over in France we  find the BJ daughters you can make your  own joke there Jess and solve must now  reclaim Paris from the Nazis and do what  their dad BJ did best suck the life out  of Nazis sorry  okay so jokes aside Wolfenstein  Youngblood introduces new mechanics to  the series with a focus on cooperative  play teamwork reviving allies and the  level design which feels more open world  than ever and less claustrophobic than  previous entries in the series although  those sections are definitely still  there this is pretty cool there's a  deluxe version of the game which allows  you to gift a copy of the game for free  to any of your friends so you can play  as the BJ twins together  Wolfenstein Youngblood releases on July  26th on ps4 PC Xbox one and switch as a  sub thought here I always feel that by  putting one of the older Wolfenstein  games on PS Plus or games with gold will  show so many new players how good these  games actually are but opinions like  this are why I'm a youtuber and they  have real jobs  [Music]  let's move our attention away from  first-person shooters and on to sea of  solitude releasing on July the 5th sea  of solitude is an action-adventure  single-player experience which looks at  mental health and in particular  loneliness in this world being alone  turns the inhabitants into monsters  there's a few unique mechanics which  deserve praise for example the weather  changes according to either the main  character's feelings or the emotions of  other characters nearby if there's a  storm brewing and things are getting  dark be careful where you go next  another mechanic is the water level  which fluctuates as Kaye understands her  emotions this game can be easily spoiled  so let's not talk anymore sea of  solitude releases on the ps4 Xbox one  and PC on July the 5th oh and sea of  solitude retails for about one third of  the price of a triple-a game so over  here in the UK it's only twenty pounds  have you ever played Dragon Quest  builders how can I explain it  it's like Minecraft to cross with a  retro Legend of Zelda title it's a  monumental success in its native Japan  on July the 12th the second game in the  series inspirationally called Dragon  Quest builders to hit stores and judging  by the firm itsu score of 37 out of 40  this is a must play I have no idea why  they score it out of 40 and not ten are  100 so let's convert that percentage  it's a ninety two point five out of 100  whoa so in addition to finding resources  and constructing buildings and equipment  builders to introduces the ability to  fly travel underwater and instantly fast  travel to interested if you have a ps4  or switch you can get your digital hands  on this on July the 12th  [Music]  do you watch stranger things no neither  do hi but at least one person a week  tells me how great it is well on July  the fourth the retro-inspired stranger  things 3 video game drops on ps4 PC Xbox  one switch iOS and Android so basically  anything that has a screen on it  inspired by the late 80s and early 90s  isometric games you're probably too  young to remember but if you're old like  me this will be like a snez nostalgia  punch to the groin the game follows the  format of season 3 of the show so once  again let's not look too deep at the  risk of spoilers July the 4th if you're  interested  Just Cause 4 gets a hit of DLC on July  the 3rd in fact if you have the gold  edition you already have early access  right now but does me immortals and  plebs need to wait until July the 3rd  just goes for the open world destruction  simulator filled with guns and carnage  returns with lost domani us which I'm  going to guess translates to the demons  this DLC is adding the supernatural to  the world and lots of neon by the looks  of things we once again fill the boots  of Rico Rodriguez and attempt to contain  this outbreak vehicles people well  basically anything that moves can be  possessed by the plants boars making  this DLC completely unique to what Just  Cause usually gets us oh and last month  there was a visual update to the entire  Just Cause 4 engine that in itself is  worth of notes shame it didn't look this  good on release day but hey onwards and  upwards los demonios is available to all  from July the 3rd on ps4 PC and Xbox one  [Music]  and to end let's look at a VR game its  Wolfenstein yet again this time though  its cyber pilot releasing on psvr  and PC through VR compatible devices on  July the 26th it's a pretty cool premise  we play as a hacker and Jack into Nazi  war machines and turn them against their  creators pretty straightforward let's  leave the final summation to Year  gustafson if you don't know what you are  missing so there we have it 7 new games  and DLCs to play over july 2019 and  beyond  does anything float your boat this month  i'm tempted to go back to apex legends  for season 2 and maybe one of those  Wolfenstein games I'm Adam from  PlayStation granade it's been a pleasure  as always if you want to talk to me come  find me on twitter i'm adam granade over  there it's been a pleasure  i'll see you next time  [Music]

